{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And who</b> — The desire of all is to live many years; therefore [it means] one who loves long days, like men of qualities, men of heart. And the meaning is: known days, like the days of so-and-so who lived thus."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The comment is textually difficult: the relation between the clauses about 'men of qualities / men of heart' and the interpretation 'known days' is unclear and possibly corrupt; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:28.919431655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}